            <ArticleTitle>[Spontaneous liver rupture in pregnancy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>819-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author reports on a rare case of spontaneous rupture of the liver during pregnancy - a rare but life-threatening event. In this particular case, the cause of the incident was probably the occurrence of a late gestosis. Early identification and, consequently, suitable surgery will usually prove life-saving.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
